abstract: >-
  Horosa for Windows v3.9.1 beta is a local-first metaphysics workstation. In astronomical
  geomancy the chosen time and place now genuinely drive the calculation: a fourth ascendant
  method casts a real chart for the selected moment and location (the only method that yields
  cusp degrees, and therefore the only one under which quadrant house division truly applies),
  a fourth planet-placement method places the seven planets and the nodes by real longitude,
  quadrant division uses the whole-sign-of-the-cusp convention that works at every latitude
  including the poles, and when time or place is incomplete the reading falls back to the
  figure-derived method and says so explicitly rather than silently substituting the current
  moment. Three defects are repaired: changing any setting or location now re-derives the
  reading immediately instead of requiring a re-cast (which used to destroy the cast in hand);
  charts cast by the number-report method are no longer silently re-cast when a school or
  setting changes; and the two real-sky methods now actually take effect (coordinates were sent
  in degree-minute notation but parsed as decimal degrees, so they silently fell back). Ce Tian
  Fei Xing gains yin/yang palace determination, birth-year納音 sixty-cycle tables, and the star
  commentary and luck-cycle verses for all nineteen configurations. Tarot fills both parallel
  meaning tracks to the full seventy-eight cards. It builds on the v3.9.0 release, which added a
  complete new technique and brings six existing modules to full coverage of their source
  classics, alongside a fidelity fix that affects every divination technique with saved records.
  The new technique is Ling Qi Jing (the Classic of Numinous Chess), the fifteenth sub-technique
  under Divination / Other: twelve pieces in three tiers (upper/middle/lower) are cast in one
  throw, with optional manual placement or direct entry of the three tier values; all 125
  hexagrams are transcribed from the Siku edition with names, piece counts, image names,
  attributes, oracle texts, four commentators, case judgments and verdict poems, in both
  simplified and original-script tracks, with three seed modes for reproducibility and a
  freeze-on-cast rule so later changes of time or display never silently recast. Six modules
  gain full classical coverage: Ce Tian Fei Xing (three switchable source readings, an annual
  outer ring, four spirit tables, twenty-eight miscellaneous star placements, a 470-rule verdict
  engine and thirteen source texts); Tarot (reversal systems 6 to 13, four parallel meaning
  tracks, spreads 30 to 65, two court-card systems, eight verdict methods, five timing methods,
  a single-card detail panel and a daily-course tab); Wu Zhao (125 verdict forms, eight casting
  methods, classical omen diagrams and a seven-page reading panel); Xiao Cheng Tu (five casting
  methods, Luoshu nine-palace layout, four timing targets and a full eight-palace text page);
  Feng Shui (two new complete schools bringing the total to seventeen, deepened form and Li Qi
  analysis, new remediation and dwelling-judgment schools, a rewritten date-selection module, a
  three-ring compass with magnetic declination for 358 cities, and automatic geometric detection
  of indoor inauspicious layouts with explicit evidence); and astronomical geomancy (eleven new
  reading techniques, eight casting methods and a dedicated planetary board). Help manuals for
  the four aggregate pages are rebuilt as two-level tabs with one page per technique. The
  fidelity fix: saving a divination result and re-loading it could previously return a different
  cast than the one saved; this is repaired across all twenty-one techniques with saved records,
  together with silent load failures, six entry points that omitted day-boundary and time-method
  settings, three techniques that were overwritten by a background refetch, and several options
  that were saved but never read back — plus a new cross-technique gate that fails the build if
  any technique omits a field. It builds on the v3.8.1 release, which brought
  "wheel art" to every Western-astrology single chart: the same chart can be drawn in five
  interchangeable styles — the classic circular wheel plus four square overlay renderings
  (a Greek nine-cell grid with the first house always the full left-middle cell; a medieval
  inscribed square with twelve triangles where houses 1/4/7/10 sit at the four edge centers,
  sign badges riding cusp midpoints on white backing and planets anchored at triangle
  centroids; a North-Indian diamond board with fixed houses and signs rotating with the
  ascendant; and a South-Indian fixed-sign grid with house numbers rotating with the
  ascendant). Planets enter their sign cells with degree-minutes and retrograde marks, Asc/MC
  are marked in red, and quadrant-system cusp projections are annotated automatically. A
  two-dropdown chart-style card (outer-ring style + wheel art) applies instantly, syncs
  app-wide, persists across sessions, and has a same-source entry in the chart-settings
  drawer. Coverage spans natal, the synastry family, the entire auxiliary-chart family
  (quantified midpoints and six-house frame, thirteenth/twelfth divisions, reset, harmonic,
  draconic and dice charts), horary, electional (including astronomical election condition
  previews), mundane, solar-term charts, firdaria, profections and prenatal syzygy;
  double-wheel overlays such as progressions/returns stay on the classic wheel. It also fixes
  auxiliary pages ignoring the chart-style selection, the quantified chart not following
  global settings, a blank wheel after switching back from square styles, and the hidden-page
  repaint mechanism failing after a wheel-art change; sign glyphs are now fixed-width so
  narrow glyphs no longer overlap degree text. It builds on the v3.8.0 release — a
  broad settings expansion across three techniques: Qi Men Dun Jia gains about forty-two new
  options including two complete standalone systems (quarter-hour Qi Men, and the day-based
  Jin Han almanac board), plus eight-spirit selection, central-palace lodging, hidden-stem
  methods, per-layer flying/rotating assembly for mixed boards, and per-school ju derivation;
  Zi Wei Dou Shu gains multi-school star-brightness sources with a user-editable brightness
  table that persists across sessions, switchable four-transformation schools, and about
  thirty-four regrouped display and luck-cycle options; Liu Yao gains eleven casting and board
  options with a full audit of all twenty-one left-panel selectors. It also rebuilds the BaZi
  twelve-growth ("chang sheng") tables to three authoritative schools so all three settings
  take effect on the main chart, fine chart, and AI snapshot; mirrors every new Qi Men option
  into the combined Three-Rites page; makes the AI analysis page open immediately by loading
  its library and session history progressively in the background; and repairs several AI
  export paths that previously reported no exportable text. It builds on the earlier release
  that completed Feng Shui to thirteen schools — deepening the
  six Liqi schools (San He twelve-growth facing / Yellow Spring & Eight Sha / Bo Sha five
  grades / Chuan Shan Tou Di gold-division lines; Qian Kun Guo Bao nine water positions; Ba
  Zhai door-master-stove with nine-star six-matters; Xuan Kong combined-facing degree
  discrimination, annual-meeting judgments and day/hour Zi Bai) and adding five new schools
  (Fu Xing hexagram-flip water method, Jing Yin Jing Yang Na Jia water method, Xuan Kong Da
  Gua sixty-four hexagrams, a landform checklist, and date selection) — with a one-screen
  thirteen-school switcher and an enlarged twenty-four-mountain compass ring; makes celebrity
  database external links open in the system browser; enriches navigation search keywords
  across sub-techniques; and permanently fixes the Tai Yi chart / unified Three Arts Tai Yi
  backend availability (with an institutional every-release availability gate covering every
  technique service). It builds on the v3.2.0 celebrity chart database — a built-in, fully
  offline catalog of tens of thousands of high-reliability A/AA-rated celebrity birth records
  with instant multi-field search and sorting (keyword / sign / gender / birth-year / Rodden
  rating / category), a detail view with a zodiac chart wheel, life events and category tags,
  and one-click import into the local chart library so any celebrity can be cast on the
  astrology / Bazi / Ziwei or any other technique page — and the Western horary chart
  expansion to five schools. It builds on the v3.1.0 release, which deepened the Xuanxue History module —
  multi-dimensional
  faceted search (tradition / dynasty / method / history) with live counts, an astronomical
  compendium (ten-year celestial-density stacks and a dynasty-by-phenomenon matrix), a
  year-by-year celestial micro-chronology with original-text and vernacular previews, a
  geographic map (dynasty heatmap + city ranking), richly-carded figures and phenomena with
  dynasty-colored tags, and a desk of bookmarks and search history persisted across restarts —
  and made the planetarium time editable (click the time to jump to any moment, recomputing
  the whole sky and chart positions live). It builds on the v3.0.0 Xuanxue History module (a standalone tools
  page compiled from public-domain classics — figures, stories, technique lineages, and
  celestial-event records — with an offline historical map, a force-directed
  figure-relationship graph, and a chronological timeline, linked to charting); broad
  multi-technique school / variant coverage across the fate and divination sets (Zi Wei, BaZi,
  Seven-Governors / Guo Lao, Western and Vedic astrology; Da Liu Ren, Qi Men, Tai Yi, Liu Yao,
  Jin Kou Jue, Tarot, Feng Shui, astronomical geomancy) surfaced as options with the default
  chart byte-for-byte unchanged; charting and AI-report enhancements; and across-the-board
  performance work. It builds on a classical/Hellenistic astrology augmentation — the natal
  chart gains a full set of classical parameters (Out of Bounds, phasis with heliacal
  rising/setting, houses of joy, day/night sect, feral, degree quality and special degrees,
  the 28 lunar mansions, apogee with number/light trends, monomoiria/ninth-part/Darijan) on a
  new Classical tab; classical configuration analysis (doryphory, overcoming, degree-besieging,
  aspect dynamics, topical almutens, accidental-dignity scoring, Behenian/Royal fixed stars,
  planetary hours, the Egyptian calendar, Babylonian reference stars, eclipse digits,
  body-part melothesia) on a Configurations tab; a sixteen-rule besiegement analysis; the AI
  analysis/export snapshot gains a Classical section kept consistent across all four mirrors
  (export/export-settings/mount/storage); and the Info tab gains a configurations overview.
  Also a high-latitude Sirius-heliacal-rising calendar fix, and AI-proxy robustness (a
  streaming worker pool and ParamHash local-cache governance) with the jar rebuilt; every
  chart computation is otherwise identical to v2.6.6. Builds on the v2.6.6 chart-math
  correction batch and primary-directions upgrade (Vertex promissor, 3000-year horizon,
  wire-protocol rev v12) plus its Windows-shell hardening pass, the v2.6.5 synastry interaction-chain
  rebuild and casting-time mounting expansion, and the v2.6.4 full-stack sidereal zodiac
  expansion (Western charts get a
  unified tropical-or-47-ayanāṃśa zodiac selector built on Swiss Ephemeris, propagated
  through the frontend, eight Java controllers, the Python chart kernel and response echo,
  and persisted storage; Western sidereal mode shows lunar mansions / Nakshatra), Indian
  astrology completion (ayanāṃśa 6→47, house systems 4→24), the four-way AI-Analysis
  synchronization with dual-chart-technique support and AI_EXPORT_SETTINGS_VERSION 23→24
  auto-migration, AI Analysis "report" generation v1, the startup-robustness pass and the
  Windows-side issue #21 fix ("本地排盘服务未就绪" now has visible health state, a rich
  error dialog, longer transparent retry, and an actionable banner). Builds further on prior planetarium
  projection refinements, the seven Western progression techniques wired into AI analysis,
  the astrocartography/ACG map, horary/electional charts, the Heluo Lishu completion, AI
  system-proxy support, the SSE service-stability fix, the global day-boundary /
  late-zi-hour model, the Ed25519-signed in-app auto-update, 数算 methods, the harmonic
  chart, clean-machine fixes, and the Windows-only NSIS installer hardening (issue #18 —
  upgrades over the top no longer fail and no longer require a manual uninstall first) — and
  AI Analysis rework, astrology modules, traditional Chinese methods, kentang/kin backend
  integrations, AI-assisted structured export, Python and Java services, and self-contained
  Windows desktop delivery into one cross-platform release line.

